{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19532-fetches-of-the-world-unite-no-okay-post-then","id":19532,"title":"Fetches of the world, unite!! ...no? Okay, post, then...?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-27T20:54:41-08:00","id":19532,"title":"Fetches of the world, unite!! ...no? Okay, post, then...?","content":"I was wondering if the peanut gallery would be willing to share with me any especially... <i>vivid </i>experiences that their characters (or STers) have had (or orchestrated) with their own (or others') fetches; The more moving (horrifying, pitiable, outlandish, etc), the better. The idea is such terrifyingly fertile ground to me, fictionally and psychologically. I'm not really looking for ideas to <i>use myself</i>, per se, just different ways that the archetype can be practically exploited or explored.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-27T22:48:54-08:00","id":19569,"title":"","content":"So I have this Spring Court NPC that I drew up for a game a while back. She was a gardener, before being taken, and was super proud of her DIY greenhouse. Well, when she got back, it turns out the she had been replaced. (Obviously.) Now, you know how Fetches lose something that the original had? Well it turns out that this fetch lost her Green Thumb. <br /> <br /> She comes back, to find the fetch desperately trying to make the flowers grow again, but its not working. NPC would have been fine to try and work things out, but she was freshly back, and this thing just killed her flowers. She reacted poorly, and stabbed her double to death with pruning shears.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/863-doctor-lazarus","name":"Doctor Lazarus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}